PURPOSE

This repository is provided as the official starter repository for COMP 330/474
Software Engineering coursework and related authorized educational use.

The repository contains instructional scaffolding, engineering templates,
repository structures, examples, workflow configuration, documentation, and
other materials intended to support student software-engineering projects.


EDUCATIONAL USE PERMISSION

Permission is granted to students enrolled in an authorized course using this
starter kit to:

- clone or fork the repository;
- modify the starter materials for their assigned project;
- add source code, tests, documentation, engineering evidence, and other
  project artifacts;
- use the resulting repository for course assignments, reviews,
  demonstrations, presentations, and assessment;
- retain their own project work after completion of the course; and
- reference or display their own original project contributions in an
  academic or professional portfolio, subject to applicable course,
  institutional, confidentiality, and third-party requirements.

Permission is also granted to authorized instructors, teaching assistants,
reviewers, and educational institutions using this starter kit to reproduce
and adapt the starter materials as reasonably necessary for course delivery,
instruction, assessment, and review.


STUDENT AND TEAM CONTRIBUTIONS

This license applies to the original starter-kit materials distributed as part
of the official COMP 330/474 starter repository.

It does not claim ownership of original source code, documentation, designs,
tests, or other materials subsequently created by students or project teams.

Student and team contributions remain subject to applicable institutional
policies, course requirements, third-party licenses, and any license selected
by the authors of those contributions.

This starter-kit license does not automatically establish a software license
for student-created project code. Teams are responsible for determining and
documenting an appropriate license before distributing their own software
outside the course when such distribution is intended.


